---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Brands from "../components/Brands.astro";
---

<Layout lang="en" title="About Us - Massive Trout Fly Fishing, Patagonia Argentina" bodyClass="no-js">
  <section class="sec__hero hero--small" id="hero_about">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__content">
        <h1 class="heading--big text--center">22 years guiding in Patagonia</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec__intro intro_sinback">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-12">
          <h2 class="heading--big text--center">About Us</h2>
          <h3 class="heading--small text--center">22 YEARS GUIDING IN PATAGONIA</h3>
          <img class="separador" src="/images/shared/separators/separador.png" alt="separador" />
          <p class="text--grey text--center">
            Massive Trout Fly Fishing is located in San Carlos de Bariloche, Patagonia, Argentina. A unique place recognized worldwide by fly fishermen not only for the fishing itself but also for the beauty of its rivers, lakes and landscapes.
            <br /><br />
            For more than 120 years, this region has provided a fabulous place for trout to reproduce, grow and live in a great number of lakes and rivers known for their superior water quality.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey text--center">
            Massive Trout Fly Fishing was established in 2009 based on three main pillars: Quality, Safety and Professionalism - to provide professional, amateur and beginner anglers an experienced fly fishing guiding service of excellence.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey text--center">
            Our team consists of professional Fly-Fishing Guides, certified to fish in the Northern Patagonia national parks; Drivers and Cargo Boys trained specifically to navigate the beautiful yet rugged lands of Patagonia and to provide specialized services and logistics, and Reservations Staff to ensure your trip is well planned based upon your desires and needs. These capabilities make Massive Trout Fly Fishing one of the top outfitters in the region.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="story-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <img src="/images/story/massive_team.jpeg" alt="Massive Trout Team" class="story-hero-img img-responsive" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container padding-top2x">
    <div class="row padding-bottom2x">
      <h2 class="heading--big text--center" id="team">Our Team</h2>
      <h3 class="about_subt text--center">EXPERIENCE AND ADVENTURE <br /></h3>
      <img class="separador_about" src="/images/shared/separators/separador_story.png" alt="separador" />

      <div class="col-md-6 text--center">
        <img class="team__avatar img-responsive img_team" src="/imagenes/story/juli_story.png" alt="Team avatar" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="team__content">
          <h3 class="team_member">Julián Cabral</h3>
          <h4 class="subt_member">Owner / Lead Guide</h4>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Julian Cabral was born in Allen Argentina and moved to Bariloche with his family at the age of 10 – which is also the age he began fly fishing. He grew up hunting and fishing in the wilderness of northern Patagonia, developing a life-long passion for the outdoors, especially fly fishing. Julian has traveled and fished throughout the region since childhood, and draws upon this knowledge to provide a once-in-a-lifetime experience for his clients.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            After earning a degree in Aquaculture with Salmonids Orientation in 2004 and additional training in rafting and scuba diving, Julian began his career as a professional fly fishing guide, first for other outfitters including Fly Fishing Patagonia and Outfitters Patagonia, where he also served as Chief of Operations, and for the Orvis-endorsed Rio Manso Lodge.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            In 2010 he founded Massive Trout Fly Fishing. Since then, Julian has successfully guided anglers from all over the world throughout Northern Patagonia in support of massive trout.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">Juilan is fluent in English</p>
          <div class="clearfix"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-6 text--center">
        <img class="team__avatar img-responsive img_team" src="/imagenes/story/cintia_story.png" alt="Team avatar" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="team__content">
          <h3 class="team_member">Cintia Acosta</h3>
          <h4 class="subt_member">Reservations & Non-Anglers Activities</h4>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Cintia Acosta has lived in Bariloche since she was three years old. After completing her studies, she began working in various aspects of her family's business, also based in Bariloche. Her combination of business experience and deep local knowledge allows her to help our clients plan their trip according to their budget, interests and desired level of adventure.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Cintia is responsible for reservations and non-anglers activities, helping our guests make the most of their time in Patagonia, whether they are looking for a single-day excursion, outdoor adventure or a multi-day camping experience.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Over the past few years, Cintia has devoted much of her free time to recreational mountaineering throughout the Bariloche area and has participated in numerous trail running races. Her firsthand knowledge of the mountains, trails, lakes and surrounding landscapes has made her our go-to person when it comes to finding out what to do beyond fishing.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            From hiking and horseback riding to scenic excursions, mountain refuges, wine tasting or simply discovering the many hidden corners of Patagonia, Cintia knows the region from a very personal perspective and can help tailor each activity to the interests and abilities of our guests.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">Cintia is married to Julian Cabral. They have two children, Uma and Franco.</p>
          <p class="team__bio">As Cintia says: "Massive Trout Fly Fishing is a family business, and we are very proud of that!"</p>
          <div class="clearfix"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container story-team">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-6 text--center">
        <img class="team__avatar img-responsive img_team" src="/imagenes/story/jorge_story.png" alt="Team avatar" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="team__content">
          <h3 class="team_member">Jorge Acosta</h3>
          <h4 class="subt_member">Logistics, Transportation & Maintenance</h4>
          <p class="team__bio">
            For more than ten years, Jorge Acosta has been an essential part of the MTFF team, overseeing logistics, transportation, and maintenance both during the fishing season and throughout the rest of the year. He also serves as the personal driver for Julián Cabral, MTFF's owner and Head Guide, a responsibility that reflects the high level of trust between them.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Originally from Buenos Aires and a resident of Bariloche for more than four decades, Jorge has an extensive knowledge of the region and a long professional background in the automotive and commercial fields. His deep understanding of the area, combined with a broad network of local contacts, makes him an invaluable asset when situations arise that require experience, efficiency, and immediate solutions.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">
            Practical, resourceful, and always ready to find a way forward, Jorge is known for his positive and proactive attitude toward both work and life. Much of what he does happens behind the scenes, but his contribution is an essential part of what makes the MTFF experience possible.
          </p>
          <p class="team__bio">We are proud to have Jorge as part of our team and look forward to sharing many more years with him.</p>
          <div class="clearfix"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-book-cta">
      <a href="/booking/" class="btn btn--full btn--oval">
        Book your trip
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Brands
    className="story-brands"
    heading="We are supported by the following brands"
    subheading="Fish with the best"
  />
</Layout>
